{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:ClimaxVolumeMass.QAngularMomentum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"ClimaxVolumeMass.QAngularMomentum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.spinHalfCasimirIllustration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.spinHalfCasimirIllustration","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/q-angular-momentum.lean#L105-L112","doc":"For spin-½ at `q ≈ 1.1097`: `[1/2]_q · [3/2]_q ≈ 0.818` (classical 0.75).\n\nThe literal is a rounded illustration, not the substrate anchor — the live\npin is `q_at()` in `qou_substrate.constants`, currently\n`1.1099785827513808`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.qNumberReal_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.qNumberReal_zero","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/q-angular-momentum.lean#L99-L103","doc":"`[0]_q = 0`: the numerator is `q⁰ - q⁰`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.qNumberReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.qNumberReal","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/q-angular-momentum.lean#L87-L97","doc":"The q-number `[n]_q = (qⁿ - q⁻ⁿ)/(q - q⁻¹)` at **real** exponents.\n\n**Deliberately not consolidated onto `QOU.QInteger.qIntBal`** (`qou-qint`\ncensus). The index `n` is a real, not a `ℕ` or a `ℤ`, and that is\nload-bearing: `qCasimir` is evaluated at `j` and `j + 1` for a *spin* `j`,\nwhich takes half-integer values. The canonical bracket and its `ℤ`-indexed\nsibling `qIntBalZ` are both discretely indexed, so neither can express this;\nthere is no equation to state, not merely none convenient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.casimir","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.casimir","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/q-angular-momentum.lean#L77-L80","doc":"The Casimir eigenvalue carried by an instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.qCasimir_zero_of_qNumber_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.qCasimir_zero_of_qNumber_zero","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/q-angular-momentum.lean#L65-L75","doc":"A q-number vanishing at `0` forces the Casimir to vanish at `j = 0`.\n\nThis is the ring-generic content of the classical limit `[n]_q → n` as\n`q → 1`: it needs no ordering, no exponentiation and no archimedean\nstructure, only that the bracket kills `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.qCasimir","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.qCasimir","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/q-angular-momentum.lean#L60-L63","doc":"The q-Casimir eigenvalue `J_q²(j) = [j]_q · [j+1]_q`, over any commutative\nring, for any q-number `qn`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.m_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.m_bound","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/q-angular-momentum.lean#L54-L54","doc":"The magnetic quantum number is bounded by `±j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.m","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.m","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/q-angular-momentum.lean#L52-L52","doc":"The magnetic quantum number `m`, ranging from `-j` to `+j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.j","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.j","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/q-angular-momentum.lean#L50-L50","doc":"Spin quantum number `j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.q","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/q-angular-momentum.lean#L48-L48","doc":"Substrate parameter `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.qNumber","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.qNumber","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/q-angular-momentum.lean#L46-L46","doc":"The q-number `[·]_q` this instance is built over. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum.mk","kind":"ctor","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/q-angular-momentum.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum","kind":"structure","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/q-angular-momentum.lean#L37-L54","doc":"**q-Angular momentum.** The q-deformed commutation relation\n`[J₊, J₋] = [2J_z]_q` (not `2J_z`), carried by a particle knot.\n\nThe q-number is a *field* rather than a fixed function, which is what keeps\nthe structure generic: the Casimir below is `[j]_q · [j+1]_q` for whichever\nbracket the instance supplies. `PartialOrder R` is required only to state\n`m_bound`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:q-angular-momentum","label":"def:q-angular-momentum","md":"quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/q-angular-momentum.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}